  "problem": "If $\\overset{\u2015}{A}={l,m,n,o}$ and $\\overset{\u2015}{B}={k,l,o,p,q,r},$ then what is $\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cup B}?$",
  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cup B}\u2261\\overset{\u2015}{A}\\cap \\overset{\u2015}{B}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cup B} & =\\overset{\u2015}{A}\\cap \\overset{\u2015}{B} \\\\  & ={l,m,n,o}\\cap {k,l,o,p,q,r} \\\\  & ={l,o}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
